{% comment %}
  AI Glasses Try-On — product page block.
  Add via theme editor: Product template → Add block → "AI Glasses Try-On".

  This just loads Lumi Frame's own widget (@lumiframe/sdk) and hands it
  this product's real data via Liquid — no custom modal/button code lives
  in this app, Lumi Frame's SDK builds and places the button itself.

  Everything about the button — label, colors, and which products it
  shows on ("Which products" tab) — is set once, for the whole store, on
  this app's own Settings page, not here. This block's only job is to
  hand tryon-widget.js this product's real data (id, title, price, and
  which collections it's in, so the "only a specific collection" setting
  has something to check against) and let the JS decide whether to show
  anything.

  This block alone only covers the button on THIS product page. The
  "Mini-card button" setting (Settings → Mini-card button tab) also needs
  tryon-embed.liquid enabled once under Theme editor → App embeds — this
  block never runs on a collection/search page, so it has no way to add a
  button to cards there on its own.
{% endcomment %}

{% liquid
  assign agto_price = product.selected_or_first_available_variant.price | default: product.price
  assign agto_price = agto_price | divided_by: 100.0
  assign agto_collection_ids = product.collections | map: 'id' | join: ','
%}

<div
  data-agto-root
  data-product-id="{{ product.id }}"
  data-product-title="{{ product.title | escape }}"
  data-product-url="{{ product.url }}"
  data-product-image="{{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 1200 }}"
  data-price="{{ agto_price }}"
  data-currency="{{ cart.currency.iso_code | default: shop.currency }}"
  data-sku="{{ product.selected_or_first_available_variant.sku }}"
  data-locale="{{ request.locale.iso_code }}"
  data-collection-ids="{{ agto_collection_ids }}"
  {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
></div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "AI Glasses Try-On",
  "target": "section",
  "javascript": "tryon-widget.js",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Everything about this button — label, colors, and which products it shows on — is set once for the whole store, on this app's own Settings page (Which products tab). Nothing to configure here."
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
